{
  "configuration_id": "config_029",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_048 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, multiprofile) is the clear best at 0.7062 acc / 0.6671 F1, a ~7-point jump over the next-best (config_005 at 0.6352) driven primarily by the scvi_n200 RNA encoder. Weighted fusion also consistently beats concat (config_005 vs config_015). The one untested dimension within this top-performing recipe is the aggregation strategy: config_048 uses avgpool, which treats all profiles symmetrically and discards inter-profile structure. Question: config_029 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) tests whether a transformer over the multiprofile sequence can capture profile-level interactions that avgpool misses, while keeping every other setting at its proven optimum. Why this is the best next experiment: it is the single most informative exploitation step—only one variable changes from the current best, so any gain or loss is cleanly attributable to aggregation. With 4 experiments left, resolving this question early lets the remaining budget focus on fine-tuning or confirming the winner. Expected relative cost: transformer aggregation over multiple profiles adds attention overhead, so I estimate roughly 10–15 GPU hours (moderately higher than config_048's 4.82 but well below config_009's 36.42), which is acceptable given the high expected accuracy payoff."
}

